# Local exclusion, loaded before the main CRS rule files run (this is
# CRS's own documented hook point for exactly this - not a guess).
#
# WordPress's Gutenberg block editor stores its block structure as raw
# HTML (comments like "<!-- wp:paragraph -->", and real tags like
# "<img>"/"<figure>" for blocks such as wp:image) inside the JSON it
# POSTs to the REST API when saving/autosaving. Two separate CRS rules
# flag this as an attack - both documented WordPress false positives,
# not actual attacks (separately verified per rule, not assumed to be
# the same report):
#   941180 - "Node-Validator Blacklist Keywords", matches the literal
#            "<!--" from block comments. coreruleset/coreruleset#1309,
#            #1618.
#   941160 - "NoScript XSS InjectionChecker: HTML Injection", matches
#            real inline tags like the <img> a wp:image block embeds.
#            SpiderLabs/owasp-modsecurity-crs#860 ("941160 FP - WordPress
#            editor add media add image") - a different, independent
#            report, not the same issue as 941180's.
#
# Scoped narrowly: only the wp-json REST API, only the two args that
# legitimately carry Gutenberg's block markup, only these two rules -
# everything else on this branch still gets checked normally.
SecRule REQUEST_FILENAME "@rx /wp-json/wp/v2/" \
    "id:1000010,\
    phase:1,\
    pass,\
    t:none,\
    nolog,\
    ctl:ruleRemoveTargetById=941180;ARGS:json.content,\
    ctl:ruleRemoveTargetById=941180;ARGS:json.excerpt,\
    ctl:ruleRemoveTargetById=941160;ARGS:json.content,\
    ctl:ruleRemoveTargetById=941160;ARGS:json.excerpt"
